    {
      "mechanism_id": "actrw_model",
      "statement": "The alternated continuous time random walk (A-CTRW) model describes particle transport as a sequence of alternating flights and dives. Flights are long-range advective segments where attachment cannot occur; dives are short segments near grain surfaces where attachment can occur at a constant rate. The model predicts the deposition profile and breakthrough curve from the distributions of flight lengths, dive lengths, velocities, and the attachment rate.",
